{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a34a9dc897175948","name":"Gambling","source":{"id":"source:reference-a34a9dc897175948","title":"Gambling","revision":18209,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T19:47:18Z","sha256":"75c3803a087bbc1e8dfb0a6ef15de2d9e35da85f48222f715ca3f658cc0784f5","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18209","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Gambling&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a34a9dc897175948","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]}," \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Characters can win or lose credits by betting on swoop races or playing games of chance, such as Sabacc and Jubilee. Use these rules whenever a character plays against the house, gambles against other characters, or takes their chances on games of pure chance.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Against the House"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["When Gambling Against the House, such as when playing the Jubilee wheel or betting on the outcome of a race, you must declare how many credits you want to wager as your stake. A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," check determines whether you win or lose, and by how much:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["WISDOM"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/WISDOM"}," CHECK\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["RESULT\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Less than 5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Lose entire stake\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5-9\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Lose half of stake\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10-14\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Break even; keep entire stake\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["15-19\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Win stake x2\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20-24\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Win stake x5\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25 or Higher\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Win stake x10\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Against Other Characters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["When Gambling against other opponents, including GM characters and other heroes, each participant declares an amount to wager and makes a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," check. The character with the highest result wins; if two participants are tied for the highest result, they split the winnings. Each participant other than the winner(s) compares their check result against the winner(s) result, using the difference in scores to determine how much money is deducted from their stake and added to the winners' stake.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DIFFERENCE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WINNINGS\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1-4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Break even; keep entire stake\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5-9\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Give 1/2 of stake to winner(s)\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10 or More\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Lose it all; give entire stake to winner(s)\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Games of Pure Chance"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["When you play a Game of Pure Chance, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," checks never come into play. Simply roll 1d20 and consult the table below:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","